  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development, by reason of its insufficient gross internal area, including two undersized bedrooms and indoor communal area, in conjunction with the lack of private outdoor amenity space, has resulted in a poor quality, cramped and compromised form of residential accommodation which would not be capable of meeting the reasonable needs of occupiers and would be detrimental to the residential amenities of future occupants. The development is thereby contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2021), Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP4 of the Core Strategy (2010), Policies DMD5 and DMD8 of the Development Management Document (2014) and the Technical Housing Standards - Nationally Described Space Standard (2015).",
    "The development, by reason of its lack of defensible space to the kitchen window serving the HMO, has resulted in a loss of privacy for the HMO, in addition to the harmful impact to the host property in terms of loss of privacy to the rear garden, as such, the existing use gives rise to poor living conditions for occupiers of the HMO, and for the occupiers of the host dwelling. The development is thereby contrary to the high-quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2021), Policy D3(7) and D6 of The London Plan (2021), Policy 4 of the Core Strategy (2010) and Policies DMD5 and DMD8 of the Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
